rve old work records and their paid progress under their recorded revision; do not silently restart or reinterpret them. Dependencies are the existing cord handler, reed strand law, personal passing-source-sample records, item reservation and persistent work/event systems. No tool, anchor, water, extra fiber, splice, or strength enhancement is supplied. Only materials supported by an executable strand law can proceed; unsupported material is a reported mechanism gap, not a fabricated result.\\\\nRequire exact owned, accessible, unreserved stacks totaling 0.2–1 unit in 0.1 steps, one fiber and source, with processing/condition covered by the actor's passing sample under the existing 0.05 tolerance. A known observation of successful cord making is not automatically mastery or a matching sample. item-225-wren-2518 is a tested-lot record to validate, not a grant of additional raw stock. Existing finished cords item-226-wren-2532 and item-250-wren-2847 cannot be reclassified as raw fiber or silently extended. Validate the supplied raw stack IDs at execution; do not infer the contents of unread inventory records. Require dry footing, sufficient clear working space and nobody within the actor's radius plus half the working cord length. Check actual hand reach, grip and ability to retain intermediate twist without external assistance. Bare-hand sequential regripping may proceed only where the implemented geometry can retain the work; otherwise pause or record the measured limitation, never assume an anchor.\\\\nFor requested twisted length L, use n=ceil(L/0.30) work sections, each at most 0.30 m, with continuous strands rather than joins. Charge n separate-align rounds, n twist rounds, n counter-ply rounds and one final release-check round, each 1 energy and one world round: 4 rounds/4 energy through 0.30 m, 7 rounds/7 energy above 0.30 through 0.60 m. Store section endpoints, actual aligned/twisted/plied lengths, held versus released geometry, stage, material allocation, condition and paid charges in the work record. Round 1 measures feasibility; charge this real attempted work even if it discovers a shortfall, but charge no unperformed later rounds. Preserve the existing 0.0005 condition loss per actual worked round, once, and its condition-at-least-0.5 release requirement. Sample remains 0.1 owned non-food unit, 1 round/0.5 energy, producing a tested lot or cracked scrap; inspect remains 1 round/0.2 energy; trial remains 1 round/0.5 energy with the existing force, duration and item limits; cancellation is free. Invalid requests cost nothing.\\\\nDerive solid volume from the actual selected material under fiber-cord@1, retaining reed's 1.8 m stems, 500 kg/m3 density, water-share treatment, wet strength and creep rather than inventing another material law. Divide actual usable solid volume equally between two plies using the existing twist take-up factor 1.155 and 0.02 m loose-end allowance. Require strand lengths sufficient for the computed ply paths, diameters within 1–12 mm, and feasible hand handling. Preserve exact length semantics: requested twisted span is not overall length including loose ends. More length at fixed usable volume means thinner plies, not free material. Record actual diameter, twisted length, overall length, condition, strand losses and twist directions. Allocate every input quantity exactly once among reserved unworked material, workpiece, returned fiber and broken scrap; volume in finished plies plus ends and scraps cannot exceed input volume. No rounding creates stock. On measured infeasibility return recoverable fiber and retain any real damage as scrap; do not label a short or incomplete piece as the requested completed product.\\\\nA completed release check creates only the supported, owned, untested cord. A shortfall reports supported dimensions and the limiting constraint; accepting any shorter unfinished work for further processing requires an explicit subsequent action. Inspect exposes only measured work/item geometry. Trial reuses fiber-cord@1 force, grip, extension, creep, damage and fragment accounting and proves only the actual force and duration. The reported 0.4332 m binding requirement is evidence for that earlier geometry, not a universal target or promise: a longer thinner cord changes width and bend geometry. Any later binding must independently execute hand-bind-crossing with exact items and recompute its wrap, closure, tails and retention under crossing-contact@1, cord-knot@1 and cord-bend@1.\\\\nUnworked rounds, insufficient energy, lost reach, unsafe footing or obstructed workspace pause before charging. Paid stage progress persists; hand-held tension may relax, and resume rechecks the physical state without claiming completion of lost twist. Any necessary real rework is explicitly charged as work, not a second charge for an unchanged completed stage. Resume with make and workId only; reject conflicting material or length arguments. Cancel or death releases unworked reservations exactly once and leaves allocated workpiece and scrap in their actual state and location; death leaves materials at the death location. Never refund spent time, energy or worked material. No automatic background fabrication runs while paused or during development. Finished cord retains ordinary material wear and any existing ongoing trial or binding processes; this extension adds no automatic repair, maintenance benefit or indefinite retained tension. All validation, accounting, state transitions and deduplication must execute in code rather than renewed model review.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":3,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"Study individually for 3 rounds at 0.2 energy per round if the applicable capability is not already learned; verified personal learning may be migrated without granting mastery merely from observations. Study, requesting, registration, inspection queries and naming give no experience reward. Keep the existing no-reward behavior for this smallest functional extension: it adds no pleasure, satisfaction, comfort or nutrition effect. Record observable practice and genuinely new measured outcomes, including informative failures, separately from rewards; repeated geometry reports are not new information. Any later experience integration must use real personally applicable events, functional deduplication, bounded awards/caps, decay and cooldown in code, and may recognize modest familiar legitimate practice without requiring novelty. Never modify protected reward accounts, budgets, goals or permissions; physical comfort remains capped at 10 and mood never reduces basic nutrition.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Emit reusable stage-progress, pause, resume, cancellation, measured-shortfall, release-result, inspection and trial events with actor ID, work/item references, revision, stage/section, paid progress, measured lengths, ply diameter, condition, actual outcome and visible material/scrap allocation. Reuse the existing fiber-cord visual representation with parameterized two-ply geometry, S/Z twist, loose ends and completion state. Display only the currently supported geometry: held or partially plied fiber must remain visibly unfinished, and failed release or shortfall cannot show a completed 0.60 m cord. A completed cord is marked untested until an actual trial; no strength badge, successful binding, hidden-resource preview or reward animation follows merely from development, study or a request.\\\"}]}\"}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":true,"prompt_cache_key":"ef753873-682f-403a-81d9-b8ddbfdddf2f","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"json_schema","name":"bounded_decision","description":null,"schema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["queries","result_json"],"properties":{"queries":{"type":"array","maxItems":4,"items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"